## Final Judgement
Based on the fact-check evidence, the key insight is that the trash cans labeled "BALLOT BOX" in Philadelphia were placed by the Union League Legacy Foundation on October 23, 2020, as an advertisement for their voting rights exhibit, not as a deliberate scheme to mislead voters into discarding ballots. The signs were removed within hours by authorities to prevent confusion with actual ballot boxes, and there is no evidence that any official ballots were discarded or that the intent was to facilitate ballot disposal.

The evidence clearly addresses the intent and circumstances of the incident, so no further investigation is needed. Therefore, I can proceed directly to a conclusion.

